[2026-03-14T23:06:27.454Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UDBRXjY9QcUynqKtJGqN2k","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now I have all the information you need. Let me compile a comprehensive report.\n\n## Summary of Assignee Selection Components and Test IDs\n\n### 1. **Assignee Selector Components**\n\nThe application has two main components that handle assignee selection:\n\n#### **IssueSidebar.tsx** (Issue Detail View)\n**Location:** `/repo/apps/LinearClone/src/components/IssueSidebar.tsx`\n\nThis is the primary assignee selector in the issue detail view.\n\n**Key Elements:**\n- **Sidebar field:** `data-testid=\"sidebar-assignee-field\"`\n- **Toggle button:** `data-testid=\"sidebar-assignee-btn\"` - displays current assignee or \"No assignee\"\n- **Dropdown container:** `data-testid=\"sidebar-assignee-dropdown\"` - opens when button is clicked\n- **Search input:** `data-testid=\"sidebar-assignee-search\"` - searchable member list\n- **Unassign option:** `data-testid=\"sidebar-assignee-option-none\"` - removes assignee\n- **Member options:** `data-testid=\"sidebar-assignee-option-${m.id}\"` - individual member options (where `m.id` is the member ID)\n\nThe dropdown displays:\n- Current assignee name with avatar (initials)\n- Search box for filtering members\n- \"Unassign\" button\n- Filtered list of team members (lines 225-235)\n\n#### **CreateIssueForm.tsx** (Create/Edit Issue)\n**Location:** `/repo/apps/LinearClone/src/components/CreateIssueForm.tsx`\n\nSimilar assignee selector used when creating new issues.\n\n**Key Elements:**\n- **Assignee field:** `data-testid=\"create-issue-assignee-field\"`\n- **Toggle button:** `data-testid=\"create-issue-assignee-selector\"`\n- **Dropdown container:** `data-testid=\"create-issue-assignee-dropdown\"`\n- **Search input:** `data-testid=\"create-issue-assignee-search\"`\n- **Unassign option:** `data-testid=\"create-issue-assignee-option-none\"`\n- **Member options:** `data-testid=\"create-issue-assignee-option-${m.id}\"`\n\n---\n\n### 2. **How Assignees Are Displayed**\n\n#### **In Issue List (IssueRow.tsx)**\n**Location:** `/repo/apps/LinearClone/src/components/IssueRow.tsx`\n\nIssues show assignee information in the list view:\n- **Assignee avatar:** `data-testid=\"issue-assignee-${issue.id}\"` (lines 260-268)\n- Displays only the initials of the assignee name (if assigned)\n- Shown in the right side of each issue row\n- Only rendered if `issue.assigneeName` is not null\n\n#### **In Issue Detail Page (IssueSidebar.tsx)**\n- Full assignee name with avatar displayed in the sidebar (lines 198-205)\n- Shows \"No assignee\" placeholder if unassigned\n\n---\n\n### 3. **Data Structure**\n\nThe Issue type includes these assignee-related fields (from `/repo/apps/LinearClone/src/slices/issuesSlice.ts`):\n```\nassigneeId: string | null\nassigneeName: string | null\nassigneeEmail: string | null\n```\n\n---\n\n### 4. **API Endpoints for Verification**\n\n#### **Issue Detail Endpoint**\n**Path:** `/repo/apps/LinearClone/netlify/functions/issue-detail.ts`\n\n- **Endpoint:** `/api/issue-detail?issueId={issueId}` (GET)\n- **Query:** Fetches full issue data including assignee (lines 45-73)\n- **Assignee data retrieved:**\n  - Joins `LEFT JOIN members m ON m.id = i.assignee_id` (line 70)\n  - Returns `m.name AS assignee_name`, `m.email AS assignee_email`, `i.assignee_id`\n  - **Critical:** Uses `LEFT JOIN` which means it will return the issue even if the member record is deleted, leaving assignee_name and assignee_email as NULL\n  - Members list for the selector fetched from `team_members` table (lines 136-142)\n\n#### **Team Issues Endpoint**\n**Path:** `/repo/apps/LinearClone/netlify/functions/team-issues.ts`\n\n- **Endpoint:** `/api/team-issues?teamId={teamId}` (GET)\n- **Retrieves all issues for a team with assignee info**\n- **Assignee data:** Same LEFT JOIN pattern (line 70)\n- **Members list:** Only includes active team members (lines 125-131)\n\n#### **Members Endpoint**\n**Path:** `/repo/apps/LinearClone/netlify/functions/members.ts`\n\n- **GET /api/members** - Lists all active workspace members\n- **DELETE /api/members/{memberId}** (lines 160-191)\n  - Removes member from `team_members` table first (line 181)\n  - Deletes sessions and member record\n  - **Critical:** Does NOT update `issues.assignee_id` field, so issues retain the assignee_id reference\n\n---\n\n### 5. **Verification Strategy for Carol's Issues After Removal**\n\nTo verify Carol persists in issues after removal:\n\n1. **Carol disappears from dropdown:**\n   - Open the assignee dropdown in an issue detail view\n   - Carol won't appear in `sidebar-assignee-dropdown` because members are fetched from active `team_members` (line 142 of issue-detail.ts)\n\n2. **Carol still shows on issues:**\n   - The issue detail shows `issue.assigneeName` from the LEFT JOIN result (lines 64-65 of issue-detail.ts)\n   - After deletion, queries will still find the `assignee_id` value pointing to Carol's record\n   - BUT her name might not display if the member record itself is deleted entirely\n   - **Better approach:** Check the issue data directly via the API response to see if `assignee_id` is still present\n\n3. **Test data-testids to verify:**\n   - `data-testid=\"issue-assignee-${issue.id}\"` - if Carol's assignee info displays in issue list\n   - `data-testid=\"sidebar-assignee-dropdown\"` - open dropdown and verify Carol is NOT in the member options\n   - Check API response payload to verify `assigneeId` still points to Carol's ID even after deletion\n\n---\n\n### Key File Locations Summary\n\n1. **IssueSidebar.tsx** - `/repo/apps/LinearClone/src/components/IssueSidebar.tsx` (assignee selector in detail view)\n2. **CreateIssueForm.tsx** - `/repo/apps/LinearClone/src/components/CreateIssueForm.tsx` (assignee selector in create/edit)\n3. **IssueRow.tsx** - `/repo/apps/LinearClone/src/components/IssueRow.tsx` (assignee display in list)\n4. **issue-detail.ts** - `/repo/apps/LinearClone/netlify/functions/issue-detail.ts` (API for fetching issue with members)\n5. **team-issues.ts** - `/repo/apps/LinearClone/netlify/functions/team-issues.ts` (API for fetching team issues)\n6. **members.ts** - `/repo/apps/LinearClone/netlify/functions/members.ts` (member management including deletion)"},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: a17f058854a9bf7f5 (for resuming to continue this agent's work if needed)\n<usage>total_tokens: 53192\ntool_uses: 17\nduration_ms: 28978</usage>"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fcb6b53d-bb9b-46d6-b424-732f94121451","uuid":"9dea2744-7e18-40e3-af5c-e9cc5a6dbdb8","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"In /repo/apps/LinearClone, find:\n1. Components that allow selecting an assignee for an issue (look for AssigneeSelect, IssueForm, issue detail, etc.)\n2. The data-testid values used in these assignee selector components\n3. How issues are displayed showing their assignee (issue list/detail views)\n4. The API endpoint for fetching issues (to verify Carol's assignments persist after removal)\n\nI need to understand how to verify that after removing Carol, her issues still show her as assigned but she's no longer in the assignee selector dropdown.","agentId":"a17f058854a9bf7f5","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now I have all the information you need. Let me compile a comprehensive report.\n\n## Summary of Assignee Selection Components and Test IDs\n\n### 1. **Assignee Selector Components**\n\nThe application has two main components that handle assignee selection:\n\n#### **IssueSidebar.tsx** (Issue Detail View)\n**Location:** `/repo/apps/LinearClone/src/components/IssueSidebar.tsx`\n\nThis is the primary assignee selector in the issue detail view.\n\n**Key Elements:**\n- **Sidebar field:** `data-testid=\"sidebar-assignee-field\"`\n- **Toggle button:** `data-testid=\"sidebar-assignee-btn\"` - displays current assignee or \"No assignee\"\n- **Dropdown container: